1
00:00:04,750 --> 00:00:06,710
What? What did you... What?

2
00:00:08,710 --> 00:00:10,300
I still love you.

3
00:00:10,550 --> 00:00:13,970
I know I shouldn't even be here telling you this.

4
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:16,430
You're with Chandler, a guy I really like.

5
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:18,600
You say he's straight, I'll believe you.

6
00:00:20,770 --> 00:00:24,600
After seeing you, I knew if I didn't tell you I'd always regret it.

7
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:27,940
Letting you go was the stupidest thing I ever did.

8
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:31,860
You're really not supposed to be back here.

9
00:00:32,530 --> 00:00:37,070
I'm sorry. I know this is the wrong time and the wrong place...

10
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:39,120
but I had to tell you.

11
00:00:39,660 --> 00:00:42,160
I want to spend my life with you and marry you.

12
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:45,750
I want to have kids with you.

13
00:00:48,330 --> 00:00:49,630
Oh, my God.

14
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,300
Why don't they put chairs back here?

15
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:57,010
I know this is crazy, but am I too late?

16
00:00:57,510 --> 00:01:00,970
Yes, you're too late. Where was all this three years ago?

17
00:01:01,220 --> 00:01:03,600
I know. I was an idiot.

18
00:01:03,850 --> 00:01:06,190
And I tried to forget you. I really did.

19
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:11,230
After we had lunch last year, I spent six months in Africa trying to forget.

20
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:14,820
What were you doing in Africa?

21
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:14,820
Working with blind kids.

22
00:01:15,070 --> 00:01:17,530
What are you doing to me?

23
00:01:18,030 --> 00:01:19,620
Look, I...

24
00:01:19,870 --> 00:01:23,410
I'm sorry, but it's not gonna happen.

25
00:01:23,660 --> 00:01:27,160
That's fine. I'll walk away. And I'll never bother you again.

26
00:01:27,420 --> 00:01:31,250
Only if you tell me Chandler's willing to give you everything I am.

27
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:34,420
Well, he is. I mean...

28
00:01:34,630 --> 00:01:36,970
marriage is all he talks about.

29
00:01:37,130 --> 00:01:38,260
My goodness.

30
00:01:38,430 --> 00:01:41,100
In fact, I'm the one making him wait.

31
00:01:41,350 --> 00:01:42,470
You are?

32
00:01:41,350 --> 00:01:42,470
Yeah.

33
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:44,640
Why?

34
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:44,640
Why?

35
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:47,560
Because of the government.

36
00:02:29,230 --> 00:02:31,350
Isn't it incredible?

37
00:02:31,650 --> 00:02:34,610
Monica and Chandler are getting married.

38
00:02:34,860 --> 00:02:37,900
I know. They'll be so happy together.

39
00:02:38,320 --> 00:02:41,030
Two best friends in love. How often does that happen?

40
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:43,240
Not that often.

41
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:43,240
No.

42
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:45,830
I'm so happy for them.

43
00:02:46,080 --> 00:02:48,500
Me too. So happy for them.

44
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:51,580
I'm so happy and not at all jealous.

45
00:02:52,170 --> 00:02:56,000
Oh, no! God, definitely not jealous.

46
00:02:52,170 --> 00:02:56,000
Mm-mm.

47
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:04,720
I'm probably 98 percent happy and maybe 2 percent jealous.

48
00:03:05,010 --> 00:03:06,510
What's 2 percent? That's nothing.

49
00:03:06,760 --> 00:03:08,270
Totally.

50
00:03:10,980 --> 00:03:13,400
I'm like 90-10.

51
00:03:10,980 --> 00:03:13,400
Yeah. Me too.

52
00:03:17,530 --> 00:03:20,360
Hey, have you guys seen Chandler?

53
00:03:23,950 --> 00:03:26,620
No. But you know who was looking for you?

54
00:03:26,830 --> 00:03:28,080
Tennille.

55
00:03:35,960 --> 00:03:38,920
So that marriage stuff you were saying yesterday?

56
00:03:39,130 --> 00:03:41,720
You don't really believe that.

57
00:03:39,130 --> 00:03:41,720
Sure, I do.

58
00:03:41,970 --> 00:03:45,550
In fact, I think the whole concept of marriage is unnatural.

59
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:49,560
Look at pigs. Let's take a second here and look at pigs.

60
00:03:50,480 --> 00:03:52,100
Pigs don't mate for life.

61
00:03:52,350 --> 00:03:55,940
A pig can have 100 sexual partners in a lifetime.

62
00:03:56,190 --> 00:04:00,190
And that's just an ordinary pig, not even a pig that's good at sports.

63
00:04:01,320 --> 00:04:02,690
Wait a minute.

64
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:06,870
Are you telling me you may never want to get married?

65
00:04:07,080 --> 00:04:09,620
Never say never, but, probably...

66
00:04:09,870 --> 00:04:11,290
yeah, never.

67
00:04:12,290 --> 00:04:13,540
Oh, my God.

68
00:04:13,790 --> 00:04:16,580
Then what are we even doing? What is this?

69
00:04:16,830 --> 00:04:20,210
Whoa, whoa, whoa, what is all this pressure?

70
00:04:20,800 --> 00:04:22,550
Is this some new strategy?

71
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:26,510
Why don't you put down your copy of The Rules, huh, man-trap?

72
00:04:28,010 --> 00:04:30,010
You know what? I gotta go.

73
00:04:32,310 --> 00:04:34,810
It's okay. I got a plan.

74
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:43,110
We're gonna find love.

75
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:43,110
Definitely.

76
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:47,320
Yeah, I'm pretty confident about that.

77
00:04:47,910 --> 00:04:52,120
That's what makes it so easy to be 80 percent happy for Monica and Chandler.

78
00:04:53,370 --> 00:04:56,290
Would be nice to have a guarantee.

79
00:04:53,370 --> 00:04:56,290
What do you mean?

80
00:04:56,540 --> 00:04:58,790
Some people make deals with a friend.

81
00:04:59,040 --> 00:05:03,630
Like if neither of them are married by 40, they marry each other.

82
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:05,510
You mean a backup?

83
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:05,510
Exactly.

84
00:05:05,760 --> 00:05:07,510
Yeah, yeah. I've got that.

85
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:10,510
You do?

86
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:10,510
Mm-hm.

87
00:05:10,760 --> 00:05:12,010
Who?

88
00:05:10,760 --> 00:05:12,010
Joey?

89
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:15,180
Joey? Are you serious?

90
00:05:12,270 --> 00:05:15,180
Yeah.

91
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:17,100
Yeah, I locked him in years ago.

92
00:05:20,270 --> 00:05:25,320
Wait. So if neither of you are married by 40, you'll marry Joey?

93
00:05:25,570 --> 00:05:27,280
Yep. We shook on it.

94
00:05:27,990 --> 00:05:31,950
Yeah. But believe me, that is not how he wanted to seal the deal.

95
00:05:33,160 --> 00:05:34,660
Seriously?

96
00:05:34,870 --> 00:05:36,830
I think his exact words were...

97
00:05:39,580 --> 00:05:40,830
Charming.

98
00:05:41,710 --> 00:05:43,840
Ah, he's just a backup.

99
00:05:41,710 --> 00:05:43,840
Yeah.

100
00:05:52,010 --> 00:05:53,220
Hey, Monica.

101
00:05:53,430 --> 00:05:55,640
Have you seen Rachel? Or a mirror?

102
00:05:57,190 --> 00:05:58,940
It's for my boat. Cool, huh?

103
00:05:59,600 --> 00:06:00,850
Yeah, it's great.

104
00:06:01,110 --> 00:06:03,610
What's the matter? Talk to the captain.

105
00:06:05,690 --> 00:06:08,990
Just realizing I'm in a dead-end relationship.

106
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:10,950
Chandler's giving you a hard time?

107
00:06:11,160 --> 00:06:14,490
I don't want to get married tomorrow. But I want to believe...

108
00:06:14,700 --> 00:06:17,750
we're going somewhere, that I'm not wasting my time.

109
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,080
You know Chandler.

110
00:06:18,000 --> 00:06:21,080
No, I don't know Chandler.

111
00:06:21,330 --> 00:06:25,420
Not anymore. It's like something's changed.

112
00:06:25,670 --> 00:06:26,920
Maybe you changed.

113
00:06:27,880 --> 00:06:29,260
I didn't change.

114
00:06:29,760 --> 00:06:31,390
Maybe that's the problem.

115
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:35,970
What?

116
00:06:33,140 --> 00:06:35,970
Chandler is a complex fellow.

117
00:06:36,220 --> 00:06:38,890
One who is unlikely to take a wife.

118
00:06:41,810 --> 00:06:45,070
Does he think I'll just wait around for nothing?

119
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:48,320
Face it. Chandler is against marriage.

120
00:06:48,570 --> 00:06:50,570
And always will be.

121
00:06:51,780 --> 00:06:54,530
Well, there's some people who do want to marry me.

122
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:57,200
There are?

123
00:06:54,740 --> 00:06:57,200
Yeah. Richard.

124
00:06:57,620 --> 00:06:59,580
Richard said he wants to marry you?

125
00:07:01,330 --> 00:07:04,290
And Chandler says he hates marriage?

126
00:07:01,330 --> 00:07:04,290
That's right.

127
00:07:05,130 --> 00:07:07,130
Chandler loves marriage!

128
00:07:09,420 --> 00:07:11,550
You just told me he hates marriage!

129
00:07:11,800 --> 00:07:15,300
That he's a complex fellow who's unlikely to take a wife!

130
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:18,100
That he's against marriage and always will be!

131
00:07:18,560 --> 00:07:20,730
You got that from what I said?

132
00:07:27,900 --> 00:07:30,400
Rach.

133
00:07:27,900 --> 00:07:30,400
Hey, you.

134
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:33,530
Hey, come on in.

135
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:33,530
Thank you.

136
00:07:34,030 --> 00:07:36,990
I'm so sorry to hear about you and Elizabeth.

137
00:07:37,240 --> 00:07:41,250
Thanks. Yeah, I really thought we'd be able to make it work.

138
00:07:41,500 --> 00:07:43,580
I guess it just wasn't meant to be.

139
00:07:43,830 --> 00:07:45,380
Yeah. Love.

140
00:07:46,210 --> 00:07:48,340
It's a tricky business, isn't it?

141
00:07:49,460 --> 00:07:50,710
I guess so.

142
00:07:51,130 --> 00:07:53,380
So, what do you say we make a pact?

143
00:07:53,630 --> 00:07:57,140
If you and I are both single by 40, we get married.

144
00:07:57,390 --> 00:08:00,430
I mean, we know each other, we like each other...

145
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:04,640
we've already slept together, so there'll be no surprises there.

146
00:08:04,900 --> 00:08:06,610
No, like, "What's that?"

147
00:08:09,900 --> 00:08:14,150
Oh, you want me to be your backup.

148
00:08:09,900 --> 00:08:14,150
Exactly.

149
00:08:14,410 --> 00:08:16,490
Oh, yeah. I already have one.

150
00:08:18,030 --> 00:08:19,280
Who?

151
00:08:18,030 --> 00:08:19,280
Phoebe.

152
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:20,790
Phoebe?

153
00:08:21,660 --> 00:08:24,410
But she just said Joey is her backup.

154
00:08:24,670 --> 00:08:26,920
Oh, I don't think so.

155
00:08:27,710 --> 00:08:31,510
I just spoke with her. She said that she and Joey made a deal.

156
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:34,670
That's impossible. We have had a deal for years.

157
00:08:34,930 --> 00:08:36,340
We shook on it.

158
00:08:36,590 --> 00:08:40,060
Although, believe me, she wanted to do a lot more than that.

159
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:45,690
Where have you been?

160
00:08:46,600 --> 00:08:49,610
I was making a coconut phone with the Professor.

161
00:08:51,570 --> 00:08:54,530
Richard told Monica he wants to marry her.

162
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:56,780
What?

163
00:08:54,900 --> 00:08:56,780
I've been looking for you.

164
00:08:57,030 --> 00:08:58,410
Stop messing with her!

165
00:08:58,660 --> 00:09:02,410
And I would have if these damn boat shoes wouldn't keep flying off!

166
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:05,210
Oh, my God!

167
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:05,210
I know! They suck!

168
00:09:06,290 --> 00:09:09,290
He's not supposed to ask her to marry him! I am!

169
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:10,920
I know!

170
00:09:09,540 --> 00:09:10,920
What...?

171
00:09:11,130 --> 00:09:14,880
You know what I'll do? I'll go over there and kick his ass!

172
00:09:15,260 --> 00:09:16,760
Will you help me?

173
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:21,600
Look, us getting our asses kicked is not a solution.

174
00:09:22,470 --> 00:09:23,680
Okay?

175
00:09:23,890 --> 00:09:27,270
Look, just go and find Monica.

176
00:09:23,890 --> 00:09:27,270
You're right.

177
00:09:27,850 --> 00:09:29,730
I'm gonna get the ring...

178
00:09:29,980 --> 00:09:31,400
I'll go find her...

179
00:09:31,820 --> 00:09:33,070
and I'll propose!

180
00:09:33,900 --> 00:09:35,240
Dude! Dude! Dude!

181
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:39,490
That coconut phone might be good for the boat.

182
00:09:55,210 --> 00:10:00,260
Hi.

183
00:10:03,140 --> 00:10:04,810
I don't know why I'm here.

184
00:10:05,520 --> 00:10:07,060
I didn't ask.

185
00:10:09,560 --> 00:10:10,980
You want to come in?

186
00:10:11,230 --> 00:10:12,650
I don't know.

187
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:15,150
Oh, okay.

188
00:10:16,030 --> 00:10:19,110
I'll just leave the door open and go sit on the couch.

189
00:10:21,700 --> 00:10:23,490
Chandler is such an idiot!

190
00:10:23,740 --> 00:10:24,990
Drink?

191
00:10:26,290 --> 00:10:28,750
Scotch on the...

192
00:10:26,290 --> 00:10:28,750
Rocks with a twist?

193
00:10:29,580 --> 00:10:31,000
I remember.

194
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:36,590
You still smoking cigars?

195
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:36,590
Uh...

196
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:39,340
No, no. That's art.

197
00:10:41,090 --> 00:10:43,430
If it bothers you, I can put my art out.

198
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:46,850
No, that's okay.

199
00:10:49,230 --> 00:10:50,810
So, Monica...

200
00:10:51,100 --> 00:10:52,810
let me ask you a question.

201
00:10:53,060 --> 00:10:55,320
Since we broke up, do you ever...

202
00:10:55,610 --> 00:10:56,820
think about me?

203
00:10:58,490 --> 00:11:01,450
Actually, I thought about you a couple months ago.

204
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:03,780
Really?

205
00:11:01,700 --> 00:11:03,780
Yeah, but it's because I...

206
00:11:04,030 --> 00:11:07,490
had an eye exam, and I don't like my new eye doctor.

207
00:11:08,830 --> 00:11:10,330
Who is it?

208
00:11:08,830 --> 00:11:10,330
Edward Nevsky.

209
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:12,040
Yeah, he's no good.

210
00:11:14,130 --> 00:11:17,300
Do you ever think about me in...

211
00:11:18,130 --> 00:11:19,670
a non-eye-doctor way?

212
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:21,220
No.

213
00:11:22,760 --> 00:11:23,970
Ah.

214
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:29,600
Because getting over you was the hardest thing I've ever had to do.

215
00:11:30,310 --> 00:11:32,480
I never let myself think about you.

216
00:11:33,600 --> 00:11:35,270
Wow.

217
00:11:40,190 --> 00:11:43,030
Phoebe, you picked Joey and Ross?

218
00:11:43,280 --> 00:11:44,950
You can't have two backups!

219
00:11:45,620 --> 00:11:47,240
Of course I can.

220
00:11:47,490 --> 00:11:50,080
It's just good sense to back up your backup.

221
00:11:50,330 --> 00:11:53,000
Look, I've already lost Chandler.

222
00:11:50,330 --> 00:11:53,000
What?

223
00:11:53,870 --> 00:11:55,170
Hey, Phoebe!

224
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:56,710
We're both backups?

225
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:59,550
How could you do this to me?

226
00:12:00,260 --> 00:12:04,430
What are you complaining about? You were both aware of the situation.

227
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:06,550
I was not!

228
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:06,550
No, we weren't!

229
00:12:06,800 --> 00:12:10,430
This kind of back talk isn't gonna fly when we're married.

230
00:12:11,310 --> 00:12:13,390
You can't have both. Pick one.

231
00:12:13,640 --> 00:12:15,100
Pick me!

232
00:12:13,640 --> 00:12:15,100
No, pick me!

233
00:12:15,350 --> 00:12:17,980
I don't want to end up an old maid.

234
00:12:19,230 --> 00:12:20,530
Well, let's see.

235
00:12:20,780 --> 00:12:22,990
Ross is a good father.

236
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:24,490
But...

237
00:12:24,740 --> 00:12:27,120
Joey has a boat. This is hard.

238
00:12:27,370 --> 00:12:29,580
This is crazy. I want to switch to Rachel.

239
00:12:29,830 --> 00:12:31,160
I want to switch too.

240
00:12:31,410 --> 00:12:33,960
No, wait! Okay, just wait!

241
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:37,210
Wait, guys. Don't make any rash decisions.

242
00:12:37,460 --> 00:12:39,460
Remember my promise:

243
00:12:39,670 --> 00:12:42,670
If we get married, three times a week.

244
00:12:42,920 --> 00:12:44,470
Oh, my God. Phoebe...

245
00:12:44,720 --> 00:12:47,090
I'm talking about massages.

246
00:12:47,340 --> 00:12:49,510
No, I'm not.

247
00:12:52,640 --> 00:12:55,350
I know how to settle this. Here's what we'll do.

248
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:57,810
I'll write "Joey"...

249
00:12:58,020 --> 00:12:59,310
on one napkin.

250
00:12:59,570 --> 00:13:02,440
And I'm going to write "Ross" on the other napkin...

251
00:13:02,690 --> 00:13:04,320
and we'll pick one.

252
00:13:04,570 --> 00:13:06,990
That person will be our backup. Here we go.

253
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:08,870
That sounds fair.

254
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:08,870
All right.

255
00:13:09,120 --> 00:13:10,660
Good. Switching them up.

256
00:13:10,910 --> 00:13:12,410
Ooh...

257
00:13:15,080 --> 00:13:16,790
Pick one.

258
00:13:15,080 --> 00:13:16,790
Left.

259
00:13:17,790 --> 00:13:19,920
Thank you.

260
00:13:17,790 --> 00:13:19,920
You're welcome.

261
00:13:22,170 --> 00:13:24,510
Ross.

262
00:13:22,170 --> 00:13:24,510
Joey.

263
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:28,800
We should just switch.

264
00:13:26,800 --> 00:13:28,800
Absolutely.

265
00:13:32,470 --> 00:13:34,310
I miss this apartment.

266
00:13:34,520 --> 00:13:36,850
Now, this is a grownup's apartment.

267
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:39,480
I should be with a grownup, you know?

268
00:13:37,100 --> 00:13:39,480
Yeah.

269
00:13:39,900 --> 00:13:44,030
You're saying you need to be with someone more mature.

270
00:13:44,610 --> 00:13:45,860
Maybe someone with...

271
00:13:47,280 --> 00:13:49,950
a license to practice medicine.

272
00:13:50,240 --> 00:13:51,950
Or a mustache.

273
00:13:53,370 --> 00:13:56,000
Let's face it. I'm not a kid anymore.

274
00:13:56,250 --> 00:13:59,120
I need to be with someone who wants the same things.

275
00:13:59,330 --> 00:14:03,710
Coming to my work and telling me you love me, I want that!

276
00:14:04,380 --> 00:14:08,090
Talking about pig sex over lunch, I don't want that!

277
00:14:09,430 --> 00:14:11,010
I think that's fair.

278
00:14:11,220 --> 00:14:14,350
Fair? Please. Don't even talk to me about fair.

279
00:14:14,600 --> 00:14:17,480
Fair would've been you wanting to marry me then.

280
00:14:17,730 --> 00:14:20,100
Or Chandler wanting to marry me now.

281
00:14:20,350 --> 00:14:23,730
Believe me, nothing about this is fair. Nothing.

282
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:26,860
Nothing! Nothing!

283
00:14:23,980 --> 00:14:26,860
It's okay.

284
00:14:27,070 --> 00:14:29,280
Hey. Shh.

285
00:14:31,240 --> 00:14:32,910
Nothing.

286
00:14:37,450 --> 00:14:40,620
I don't know.

287
00:14:41,750 --> 00:14:43,000
I know.

288
00:14:44,670 --> 00:14:46,460
Yeah, I... I...

289
00:14:47,170 --> 00:14:49,630
I have to figure...

290
00:14:49,880 --> 00:14:52,470
some stuff, before I can...

291
00:14:52,680 --> 00:14:54,180
Yeah, I understand.

292
00:14:55,310 --> 00:14:57,520
Take as much time as you want.

293
00:14:58,430 --> 00:15:00,390
Ten, 20 minutes, if you need it.

294
00:15:02,150 --> 00:15:04,860
I'll be here. Not smoking.

295
00:15:20,580 --> 00:15:23,170
Chandler.

296
00:15:20,580 --> 00:15:23,170
Where is she?

297
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:25,290
I'm not scared of you.

298
00:15:27,170 --> 00:15:29,840
She's not here. And please come in.

299
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:32,550
Scotch on the rocks...

300
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:35,180
with a twist, on a coaster.

301
00:15:35,430 --> 00:15:36,930
Monica? Monica?

302
00:15:38,810 --> 00:15:41,180
Okay, she was here. But she left.

303
00:15:41,440 --> 00:15:42,810
Where did she go?

304
00:15:43,060 --> 00:15:45,560
She said she had to think things over.

305
00:15:45,940 --> 00:15:50,190
Oh, my God. I can't believe this. I thought you were a good guy.

306
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:52,200
Oh, hey. Look, nothing happened.

307
00:15:52,450 --> 00:15:56,320
Nothing happened? Nothing? You didn't tell her you love her?

308
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:59,240
Well, all right, one thing happened.

309
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:01,330
You know what you did?

310
00:16:01,540 --> 00:16:03,830
My girlfriend is thinking things over.

311
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:06,290
You made my girlfriend think!

312
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,670
Well, I'm sorry.

313
00:16:11,010 --> 00:16:12,920
What's to think about? I love her.

314
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:17,220
Well, apparently I'm willing to offer her things that you are not.

315
00:16:17,470 --> 00:16:20,810
I'm willing to offer her those things. This was just a plan.

316
00:16:21,060 --> 00:16:25,600
To throw her off so when I offered all these things, she'd be surprised.

317
00:16:26,770 --> 00:16:29,820
If it helps, it worked very well.

318
00:16:30,730 --> 00:16:33,860
It was working till you showed up, you big tree.

319
00:16:36,570 --> 00:16:38,450
This isn't fair.

320
00:16:38,700 --> 00:16:42,120
You had your chance with her, and you blew it!

321
00:16:42,370 --> 00:16:44,500
This is my chance and I won't blow it...

322
00:16:44,710 --> 00:16:47,000
because we are meant for each other.

323
00:16:47,210 --> 00:16:50,550
And this has all just been one stupid mistake!

324
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:53,460
I was gonna propose tonight.

325
00:16:56,340 --> 00:16:57,590
You were?

326
00:16:58,430 --> 00:16:59,930
Yeah, I even...

327
00:17:00,850 --> 00:17:02,100
got a ring.

328
00:17:02,810 --> 00:17:04,310
Did you get a ring?

329
00:17:04,640 --> 00:17:06,270
No, I don't have a ring.

330
00:17:11,900 --> 00:17:13,150
You go get her.

331
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:19,120
And can I give you a piece of advice?

332
00:17:19,410 --> 00:17:21,200
If you do get her...

333
00:17:22,290 --> 00:17:23,950
don't let her go.

334
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:25,620
Trust me.

335
00:17:28,580 --> 00:17:32,050
You know, Richard, you are a good guy.

336
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:35,800
I know.

337
00:17:36,930 --> 00:17:38,340
I hate that.

338
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:54,230
Dude.

339
00:17:52,440 --> 00:17:54,230
I've gotta find Monica.

340
00:17:54,400 --> 00:17:55,440
She's gone.

341
00:17:55,900 --> 00:17:59,240
What?

342
00:17:55,900 --> 00:17:59,240
She had a bag and she left.

343
00:17:59,490 --> 00:18:01,450
What?

344
00:17:59,490 --> 00:18:01,450
She was crying.

345
00:18:01,700 --> 00:18:04,910
She said you want different things and she needs to think.

346
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:07,540
Why didn't you tell her it was a plan?

347
00:18:07,790 --> 00:18:11,040
I did! I told her everything. She wouldn't believe me.

348
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:12,420
Well, where...?

349
00:18:12,630 --> 00:18:13,880
Where did she go?

350
00:18:14,130 --> 00:18:16,670
To her parents'. She said you shouldn't call.

351
00:18:16,920 --> 00:18:19,380
But if I were you, I would.

352
00:18:20,050 --> 00:18:21,590
Can't believe I ruined this.

353
00:18:21,970 --> 00:18:24,180
I am so sorry, man.

354
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:37,360
You wanted it to be a surprise.

355
00:18:47,750 --> 00:18:49,330
Oh, my God.

356
00:18:55,960 --> 00:18:57,340
Chandler...

357
00:18:58,800 --> 00:19:00,680
in all my life...

358
00:19:01,510 --> 00:19:04,010
I never thought I would be so lucky...

359
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:11,310
as to fall in love with my best...

360
00:19:12,650 --> 00:19:14,230
My best...

361
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:19,070
There's a reason why girls don't do this!

362
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:19,070
Okay, okay, okay.

363
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:21,950
I'll do it. I thought...

364
00:19:26,200 --> 00:19:27,830
Wait, I can do this.

365
00:19:31,830 --> 00:19:34,880
I thought that it mattered...

366
00:19:35,090 --> 00:19:38,630
what I said or where I said it.

367
00:19:39,340 --> 00:19:41,340
Then I realized...

368
00:19:41,800 --> 00:19:44,890
the only thing that matters is that you...

369
00:19:48,520 --> 00:19:52,850
You make me happier than I ever thought I could be.

370
00:19:55,980 --> 00:19:58,020
And if you let me...

371
00:19:58,690 --> 00:20:02,820
I will spend the rest of my life trying to make you feel the same way.

372
00:20:11,830 --> 00:20:13,460
Monica...

373
00:20:15,380 --> 00:20:16,710
will you marry me?

374
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:20,550
Yes.

375
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:36,770
I knew you were likely to take a wife!

376
00:20:39,780 --> 00:20:42,280
Can we come in yet? We're dying out here!

377
00:20:43,450 --> 00:20:45,070
Come in! Come in!

378
00:20:47,120 --> 00:20:48,910
We're engaged!

379
00:20:54,160 --> 00:20:55,410
Oh!

380
00:20:55,670 --> 00:20:58,710
This is the least jealous I've ever been!

381
00:20:59,340 --> 00:21:02,380
Oh, no, wait! This is wrong! Ross isn't here!

382
00:21:02,670 --> 00:21:03,840
Oh.

383
00:21:02,670 --> 00:21:03,840
Oh.

384
00:21:04,510 --> 00:21:07,390
He's done it three times. He knows what it's about!

385
00:21:07,680 --> 00:21:09,430
Yeah.

